WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.920
Have you ever had an

2
00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.600
agent build exactly what you asked for, and it still looked completely wrong?

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.720
Hi, I'm Hamza, and I lead design here at Tessl.

4
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.640
This November, I'm speaking at AI DevCon New York about

5
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:13.640
automating design quality into software factories.

6
00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:16.560
Before I was a product designer, I was a mechanical engineer

7
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.080
working in real factories.

8
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.080
Factories learned the hard way that you can't inspect quality

9
00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.800
at the end of a production line.

10
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.880
Instead, you have to build it into the line itself.

11
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.960
And software factories have the exact same problem.

12
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.920
In my talk, I'll walk through the four places

13
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.440
we now catch design defects in Kikimora, our software factory here at Tessl.

14
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:40.040
They run from style rules that agents read before they build anything,

15
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.760
through checks in CI, to agents that sweep the whole product

16
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.000
looking for drift.

17
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.840
I'll show you what each one caught and, crucially, what it means.

18
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.960
You'll come away knowing how to get agents to actually follow your design guidance

19
00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.360
and how your job may evolve once they're doing all that making.

20
00:00:56.480 --> 00:01:00.440
If you're a designer, a product manager, or a front-end engineer, and agents

21
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.280
are shipping UI faster than anyone can review it, this one's for you.

22
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:07.560
You can also get 30% off your ticket with my code

23
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.880
HAMZA30.

24
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.560
Looking forward to seeing you in New York very soon.
